#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1300 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "Pins the `Requirements.Variables.All: [DOMAIN]` guard added in the same edit as the wave-15 `dataset_domain` migration (never as a follow-up). The guard is NOT cosmetic: `dataset_domain` falls back to the raw DATASET NAME when no `DOMAIN` cell can be read, so on a `DOMAIN`-less dataset whose name is not two characters the length check would fire on conformant data — a new over-report the migration would otherwise ship. ⚑ The neuter-and-watch is UNMASKED here: the class is FINDINGS so `Classes.Exclude: [RELATIONSHIP]` does not bite, and `LB` matches neither `AP--` nor `APRELSUB`, so the `Variables` block is the ONLY filter that can reject this dataset. Remove it and the rule runs. (Mirrors `CDISC-CG0308-skipped-no-DOMAIN-column-LB.cdt`, the equivalent pin on this rule's CDISC twin.)"
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results (DOMAIN variable omitted)"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
---
S1 | 01-701-1015 | ALB
S1 | 01-701-1023 | ALT
---
